      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "District 3 is the most dangerous hotspot due to its high density, reliance on public transit, and lack of primary care access, which disproportionately affects Black communities. District 2 is also a critical risk area because its large Hispanic/Latino population and service industry workforce create conditions ripe for rapid spread. These demographics are inherently more vulnerable due to systemic neglect and lower socioeconomic status.",
